    "raw": "Let's denote the original price of the DVDs as \\( P \\). Maria received a 25% discount, which is equivalent to \\( 0.25P \\). According to the problem, this discount amount is $40. Therefore, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[ 0.25P = 40 \\]\n\nTo find the original price \\( P \\), we solve for \\( P \\):\n\n\\[ P = \\frac{40}{0.25} = 160 \\]\n\nSo, the original price of the DVDs was $160. Since Maria received a 25% discount, she paid 75% of the original price. We can calculate the amount she paid as follows:\n\n\\[ \\text{Amount paid} = P - 0.25P = 0.75P = 0.75 \\times 160 = 120 \\]\n\nThus, Maria paid a total of $120.\n\nFINAL: 120",
